      ],
      "source": "https://www.ayto-alcorcon.es/en/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Legend says Alcorcón began as a watchtower on a hill, guarding Christian troops and protecting nearby Arab cities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ayto-alcorcon.es/en/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Founded in 1971, AD Alcorcón plays in Primera Federación and hosts matches at the 5,100‑seat Municipal de Santo Domingo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AD_Alcorc%C3%B3n"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2009, Alcorcón stunned Real Madrid by beating them 4–0 at home in the Copa del Rey first round.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AD_Alcorc%C3%B3n"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "That same year, Alcorcón earned promotion to Spain’s second division after defeating Pontevedra and Ontinyent in the playoffs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
